Z||000000||maninblack||08-27-2000||05:13 AM||||anyone experance this before?.My 87se 2.8 5sp<BR>have a strange idling problem.After the engine is hot,whenever I stop for a stop sign or red lite,the idling would not hold <BR>steady,usually moves between 900rpm-1100rpm.<BR>I have tried a few things already,which are<BR>replacing the idling valve sensor,tps sensor,<BR>blead the cooling system a few time for bubbles.Still it didnt solve the problem.anyone can help? thx||||reg||9
Z||000001||mshill||08-27-2000||12:21 PM||||I have a similar problem with the V6 in my 86SE.  It is not the EGR valve, tube or soleniod as I have replaced all of them.  I have a new MAT, MAP and engine coolant sensor as well.<P>I have not replaced the Idle Air Control valve yet.  I am suspecting that I may have a bad ground somewhere, but I double checked all of those when I rebuilt the engine last January.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||08-27-2000||02:04 PM||||I used to have that problem, turned out to be the EGR valve.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000003||maninblack||08-27-2000||03:50 PM||||thx guys,i will replace my mat sensor and o2<BR>sensor tomorrow and see what happens,will update you guys later,but thx||||reg||1
